. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3 * 
. 
.         * I run a fixed effects model. I assume that gender equality behaviou
> r can be measured through the division of care work 
.         * measured by the ratio of women's versus men's hours per week spent 
> on three different care work tasks: housework (pli0043_h) care work (pli0046)
>  and childcare (pli0044_h). 
.         * The variable is the ratio based on hours per week. 
.         * A value >1 means the women performs more care work, a value <1 mean
> s the women performs less care work. A value of 1 represents an equal distrib
> ution of care work. 
.         * I run a fixed-effects model with standard errors clustered at the h
> ousehold level.
.         * The constructed variable careRatio is the dependent variable and th
> e dummy variable hadDaughter is the independent variable. 
.         * I also include year fixed effects in the model.  
.         
.         xtset hid syear // deviation from PAP: accidentally put down pid wher
> e hid was meant

Panel variable: hid (unbalanced)
 Time variable: syear, 2001 to 2020, but with gaps
         Delta: 1 unit

.         sort hid syear

.         xtreg careRatio hadDaughter i.syear, fe vce(cluster hid) // deviation
>  from PAP_ birthOrder variable is not included as I only look at firstborn ch
> ildren 

